			/* Edge fade as two plain opaque gradient layers, not a CSS mask.
			   mask-image on a container with an animating transform inside it
			   is a known Chromium/GPU compositing trap on some drivers — the
			   whole masked layer can silently stop painting (exactly what
			   "the names don't show at all" looks like). Regular background
			   layers can't hit that bug: they're always just painted content. */
			.logos-fade {
