			.logos-track {
				list-style: none;
				margin: 0;
				padding: 0;
				display: flex;
				flex-wrap: nowrap;
				width: max-content;
				will-change: transform;
				/* Single shorthand declaration, all sub-values !important.
				   global.css's reduced-motion block sets animation-duration
				   AND animation-iteration-count as separate !important
				   longhands on `*` — overriding only one of them (as a prior
				   version of this rule did) leaves the other in force, so the
				   animation plays its 0.01ms single iteration and then just
				   freezes on a mid-scroll frame: a static, "broken" list.
				   Shorthand !important here re-asserts every sub-property
				   (duration, iteration-count, timing-function, name) in one
				   go, so none of them can be left behind. This is purely
				   decorative, peripheral motion (a logo strip, not core
				   content), so keeping it running under prefers-reduced-motion
				   is an intentional, scoped exception. */
				animation: logos-scroll 28s linear infinite !important;
